submission) can be completed end-to-end using\n  keyboard input alone.\n- Every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit for these flows is\n  resolved, or explicitly documented as waived with a stated reason.\n- No focus traps remain: focus can always be moved into, within, and out of\n  every modal and container in the audited flows, and focus is restored\n  sensibly when a modal closes.\n- No interactive control in the audited flows is unreachable or inoperable\n  via keyboard.\n- Focus indicators are visible and consistent across all interactive controls\n  in the audited flows.\n- Existing keyboard interactions in the four flows continue to work (no\n  regressions introduced by the remediation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | Full — the four audited core flows fully operable by keyboard, no focus traps, no unreachable controls |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Full — visible focus indicators consistent across the audited flows. Bundled with HLR-1: both requirements are remediated by the same pass over the same surfaces (modals, focus management, interactive controls) in the same four flows; splitting them would double-touch every remediation site |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24086,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1b8aa6793b78517","agent_id":"a823f6972bb4e9fce","session_id":"3c15607e-d725-4314-98f0-bc670c890834","uuid":"48d035e8-9107-423d-8307-50c769338776","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:09:03.648Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017"}
