{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93d5bc1c6b19961f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n3\tepic_count: 2\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9017\n11\t\n12\tKeyboard accessibility conformance for core Dashboard flows.\n13\t\n14\t## Triage\n15\t\n16\tNot below-threshold and not docs-only. Although the code scope is a single\n17\tcomponent (Dashboard) owned by a single team with an audit enumerating the\n18\tdefects, the strategy spans two architecturally distinct work streams that\n19\twarrant separate PR review cycles: Dashboard code remediation (HLR-1, HLR-2)\n20\tand substantive accessibility conformance content authoring — the VPAT and the\n21\tproduct docs accessibility statement, updated and republished (HLR-3). The\n22\tpublished conformance statement is an explicit deliverable tied to customer\n23\trenewal, not an incidental doc touch-up. Full decomposition follows.\n24\t\n25\t## Epic List\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | Update and republish accessibility conformance documentation (VPAT and accessibility statement) | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P2 |\n31\t\n32\t## Dependency DAG\n33\t\n34\t```mermaid\n35\tgraph TD\n36\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9017-E001: Dashboard keyboard accessibility remediation]\n37\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-9017-E002: VPAT and accessibility statement republish]\n38\t    E001 --> E002\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\t## DAG Justification\n42\t\n43\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n44\t|------|------|-----------|\n45\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | The VPAT and accessibility statement must describe the fixed state, so the docs-authoring epic is blocked by the Dashboard remediation epic. |\n46\t\n47\tNo other edges: single implementation epic for the code work (same component,\n48\tsame team, same logical change — audit-driven keyboard/focus remediation), and\n49\tno Investigation epics (the strategy's open questions table is explicitly\n50\t\"None — the audit report enumerates the exact defects per flow\", so there are\n51\tno unknowns whose resolution would change which epics exist or what they do).\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n54\t\n55\t| HLR | Priority | Epic | Coverage |\n56\t|-----|----------|------|----------|\n57\t| HLR-1 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Full — keyboard operability, no focus traps, no unreachable controls across the four audited flows |\n58\t| HLR-2 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E001 | Full — consistent visible focus indicators across the audited flows. Bundled with HLR-1: both HLRs edit the same surfaces (modals, focus management, interactive controls) in the same four flows for the same component and team; splitting would double-touch every remediation site |\n59\t| HLR-3 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9017-E002 | Full — VPAT and product docs accessibility statement updated, republished, technically reviewed |\n60\t\n61\tAll three HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n62\t\n63\t## Component Mapping\n64\t\n65\t- **Dashboard** → canonical component `Dashboard` (verbatim from\n66\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt`). Active component: code changes to the four\n67\t  audited flows. Owning team per `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`:\n68\t  RHOAI Dashboard.\n69\t- **Documentation** → canonical component `Documentation` (verbatim from\n70\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt`). Content authoring work stream: VPAT update\n71\t  and accessibility statement republish, routed as `docs-authoring`.\n72\t\n73\t## Priority Derivation\n74\t\n75\t- E001: P1 — inherits the P1 priority of HLR-1 and HLR-2, the highest-priority\n76\t  HLRs it covers.\n77\t- E002: P2 — `docs-authoring` priority exception: strategy frontmatter\n78\t  `priority: Normal` maps to P2. Per the exception, this epic does not push its\n79\t  priority upstream to E001.\n80\t\n81\t## Health Warnings\n82\t\n83\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n84\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n85\t  Non-Functional Requirements section. The decomposition proceeds from the\n86\t  HLR table, Affected Components list, and problem statement. Team assignment\n87\t  for the documentation epic is an assumption: with no Impacted Teams table,\n88\t  the docs-authoring epic is assigned to RHOAI Dashboard (the team that owns\n89\t  the fixes and must provide the technical review); reassign if a dedicated\n90\t  documentation team owns the accessibility statement.\n91\t- **Epic size overage kept deliberately**: E001 covers keyboard/focus\n92\t  remediation across all four audited flows in one epic. It is kept as one\n93\t  epic because it is one logical change (audit-enumerated keyboard and focus\n94\t  defect remediation of the same kind on the same console) for one component\n95\t  and team; a split would fragment a single mechanical pass over shared focus\n96\t  management surfaces. **Re-split trigger**: re-split along flow boundaries\n97\t  (one epic per audited flow, or code-flow fixes vs. shared focus-indicator\n98\t  work) if the audit's enumerated defect list is materially larger than the\n99\t  estimate or if any single flow's remediation exceeds roughly one week of\n100\t  effort, so that review cycles can proceed in parallel.\n101\t- **Passive validation note**: no passive components — both affected\n102\t  components have deliverables in this strategy.\n103\t- **External commitment risk (not a DAG dependency)**: the published VPAT is\n104\t  required by two public-sector customers before renewal. The renewal deadline\n105\t  is a business constraint on scheduling, not an epic dependency; it is\n106\t  recorded here for planning awareness.\n107\t\n108\t## Tiered Delivery\n109\t\n110\tNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing. Both epics are\n111\tinternally scheduled; the documentation epic simply follows the code work.\n112\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-932ce89d49d16a50","agent_id":"afcefd71f45de3f50","session_id":"3c15607e-d725-4314-98f0-bc670c890834","uuid":"6616f273-f1de-422d-940d-90e9a327da73","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:10:03.984Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93d5bc1c6b19961f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
