{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdc82e14ea5c102b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9017-E001\n3\ttitle: Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9017\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the keyboard accessibility fixes identified by the\n34\taccessibility audit for the four core Dashboard flows: project creation,\n35\tworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission. After this\n36\tepic, each of the four flows can be completed end-to-end with keyboard alone,\n37\twith no focus traps, no unreachable controls, and consistent visible focus\n38\tindicators. This is the code-remediation deliverable of the strategy; the\n39\tupdated published conformance documentation is tracked separately.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Remediate every keyboard-operability defect enumerated in the accessibility\n44\t  audit for the four audited flows, including:\n45\t  - Focus loss in modals (focus must be moved into, contained within, and\n46\t    returned from modal dialogs correctly).\n47\t  - Controls that are unreachable via keyboard (all interactive controls in\n48\t    the audited flows must be operable without a pointer).\n49\t  - Focus traps where focus becomes stuck in a container and cannot escape.\n50\t- Make focus indicators consistent and clearly visible across all interactive\n51\t  controls in the audited flows, in line with the audit's findings on\n52\t  inconsistent indicators.\n53\t- Verify that remediation does not regress existing keyboard behavior in the\n54\t  four flows.\n55\t- Out of scope per the strategy: screen-reader semantics beyond what the\n56\t  keyboard fixes require, and flows outside the four audited ones.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n61\t  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using\n62\t  keyboard input alone.\n63\t- Every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit for these flows is\n64\t  resolved, or explicitly documented as waived with a stated reason.\n65\t- No focus traps remain: focus can always be moved into, within, and out of\n66\t  every modal and container in the audited flows, and focus is restored\n67\t  sensibly when a modal closes.\n68\t- No interactive control in the audited flows is unreachable or inoperable\n69\t  via keyboard.\n70\t- Focus indicators are visible and consistent across all interactive controls\n71\t  in the audited flows.\n72\t- Existing keyboard interactions in the four flows continue to work (no\n73\t  regressions introduced by the remediation).\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n78\t|-----|----------|----------|\n79\t| HLR-1 | P1 | Full — the four audited core flows fully operable by keyboard, no focus traps, no unreachable controls |\n80\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Full — visible focus indicators consistent across the audited flows. Bundled with HLR-1: both requirements are remediated by the same pass over the same surfaces (modals, focus management, interactive controls) in the same four flows; splitting them would double-touch every remediation site |\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":